WEBVTT

1
00:01:13.458 --> 00:01:17.708


2
00:01:17.708 --> 00:01:21.125
<b>An ocean of dilemmas</b>
<b> is surging in Arjuna's mind, </b>

3
00:01:21.125 --> 00:01:26.291
<b>In these verses, he's explaining his reasons</b>
<b>for not wanting to fight. </b>

4
00:01:26.291 --> 00:01:27.375
<b>He says</b>

5
00:01:27.375 --> 00:01:31.833
<b>that on both sides of this war</b>
<b>are my own relatives, my loved ones. </b>

6
00:01:31.833 --> 00:01:38.083
<b>If they don't survive, no joy will come from</b>
<b>winning this war or gaining this kingdom.</b>

7
00:01:38.750 --> 00:01:42.958


8
00:01:42.958 --> 00:01:45.375
<b>Krishna hasn't said anything yet,</b>

9
00:01:45.375 --> 00:01:47.291
<b>hasn't given any response,</b>

10
00:01:47.291 --> 00:01:49.333
<b>nor made any argument,</b>

11
00:01:49.333 --> 00:01:54.333
<b>he's just looking at Arjuna with a gentle smile,</b>

12
00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:55.416
<b>But</b>

13
00:01:55.416 --> 00:01:58.083
<b>Arjuna is telling him every reason</b>

14
00:01:58.083 --> 00:02:03.083
<b>here to prove that his fighting</b>
<b>this war would be wrong.</b>

15
00:02:03.083 --> 00:02:05.500
<b>This happens to us too sometimes,</b>

16
00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:08.708
<b>that we start arguing with</b>
<b>someone else in our minds.</b>

17
00:02:08.708 --> 00:02:11.583
<b>We ask questions on behalf of that person, </b>

18
00:02:11.583 --> 00:02:13.625
<b> and we answer them ourselves. </b>

19
00:02:13.625 --> 00:02:17.500
<b>The debate in the mind is going on</b>
<b>as if there were two people. </b>

20
00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.250
<b>In such cases, we're not arguing with</b>
<b>anyone else, but with ourselves</b>

21
00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.000
<b>Here too,</b>

22
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.666
<b>there are such questions and answers...</b>

23
00:02:25.666 --> 00:02:28.125
<b>where Arjuna is on both sides,</b>

24
00:02:28.125 --> 00:02:32.666
<b>but it feels in his mind as if he's</b>
<b>arguing with Krishna.</b>

25
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:33.708
<b>O Krishna,</b>

26
00:02:33.708 --> 00:02:37.041
<b>there's no meaning in this kingdom, this wealth</b>

27
00:02:37.041 --> 00:02:39.250
<b>Won't these bring you happiness?</b>

28
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.375
<b>But,</b>

29
00:02:40.375 --> 00:02:46.833
<b>humans acquire wealth, fame, kingdom for their</b>
<b>loved ones, their family, don't they?</b>

30
00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:51.500
<b>If those very people die or get injured here</b>
<b>on the battlefield,</b>

31
00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:55.208
<b>what's the use of such a</b>
<b>kingdom, wealth, and fame?</b>

32
00:02:55.208 --> 00:02:57.791
<b>But you'll survive, won't you?</b>

33
00:02:57.791 --> 00:03:00.333
<b>What will I do by surviving, Krishna?</b>

34
00:03:00.333 --> 00:03:03.875
<b>If my family, my close ones aren't there?</b>

35
00:03:03.875 --> 00:03:05.083
<b>But</b>

36
00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:07.000
<b> you're a Kshatriya,</b>

37
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:09.875
<b>and this war is your duty.</b>

38
00:03:09.875 --> 00:03:13.458
<b>And in war, only the enemy is in front, isn't it? </b>

39
00:03:13.458 --> 00:03:14.500
<b>Enemy?</b>

40
00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:15.916
<b>How are they enemies, Krishna?</b>

41
00:03:15.916 --> 00:03:18.250
<b>All these are my teachers, grandfathers,</b>

42
00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:19.625
<b>father-like elders,</b>

43
00:03:19.625 --> 00:03:21.125
<b>son-like youngsters,</b>

44
00:03:21.125 --> 00:03:24.041
<b>maternal uncles, youths</b>
<b>of my grandchildren's age, </b>

45
00:03:24.041 --> 00:03:25.166
<b>all of them.</b>

46
00:03:25.166 --> 00:03:27.083
<b>And these people are on both sides.</b>

47
00:03:27.083 --> 00:03:28.875
<b>What friend and what enemy?</b>

48
00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:33.666
<b>They'll all either die or be injured.</b>

49
00:03:33.666 --> 00:03:35.583
<b>But, the people standing in front?</b>

50
00:03:35.583 --> 00:03:36.583
<b>These Kauravas?</b>

51
00:03:36.583 --> 00:03:41.666
<b>The teachers and relatives supporting them?</b>
<b>Won't they be merciless? </b>

52
00:03:41.666 --> 00:03:45.541
<b>If not you, won't they kill you? </b>

53
00:03:45.541 --> 00:03:47.125
<b>Even if they kill me,</b>

54
00:03:47.125 --> 00:03:48.291
<b>it's fine.</b>

55
00:03:48.291 --> 00:03:50.208
<b>I won't be able to kill them.</b>

56
00:03:50.208 --> 00:03:50.666
<b>But</b>

57
00:03:50.666 --> 00:03:53.916
<b>the Kauravas have always done you wrong? </b>

58
00:03:53.916 --> 00:03:55.416
<b> Will you let them go?</b>

59
00:03:55.416 --> 00:03:57.958
<b>Will you let them take such a large kingdom? </b>

60
00:03:57.958 --> 00:03:59.916
<b>Whether it's this large kingdom,</b>

61
00:03:59.916 --> 00:04:02.583
<b>or lordship over the three worlds.</b>

62
00:04:02.583 --> 00:04:06.833
<b>Is all this so big that</b>
<b>I should kill my own relatives? </b>

63
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:08.833
<b>This just can't happen.</b>

64
00:04:08.833 --> 00:04:11.458
<b>I won't be able to fight this war.</b>

65
00:04:12.083 --> 00:04:16.208


66
00:04:16.208 --> 00:04:17.750
<b>Just as </b>

67
00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:19.291
<b> the pole star</b>

68
00:04:19.291 --> 00:04:24.416
<b>shows the way to a sailor</b>
<b>in the middle of the ocean,</b>

69
00:04:24.416 --> 00:04:29.916
<b>Just as burning coal provides</b>
<b>momentum to a train,</b>

70
00:04:29.916 --> 00:04:32.000
<b>In the same way,</b>

71
00:04:32.000 --> 00:04:36.625
<b>the inspiration within us shows us the way,</b>

72
00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:40.666
<b>and gives us the momentum</b>
<b>to walk on that very path.</b>

73
00:04:40.666 --> 00:04:42.791
<b>But</b>

74
00:04:42.791 --> 00:04:48.250
<b>what if the pole star disappears,</b>

75
00:04:48.250 --> 00:04:51.208
<b>then the sailor will be lost;</b>

76
00:04:51.208 --> 00:04:54.083
<b>if the coal runs out,</b>

77
00:04:54.083 --> 00:04:58.250
<b>the train will stop right there.</b>

78
00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:02.041
<b>If our inspiration is lost somewhere,</b>

79
00:05:02.041 --> 00:05:06.875
<b>then we too will stop there directionless</b>

80
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:08.458
<b>even if we have</b>

81
00:05:08.458 --> 00:05:10.250
<b>every means of life,</b>

82
00:05:10.250 --> 00:05:13.875
<b> every happiness.</b>

83
00:05:13.875 --> 00:05:17.541
<b>The same thing is happening with Arjuna.</b>

84
00:05:17.541 --> 00:05:22.500
<b>The inspiration within him for</b>
<b>the war is weakening</b>

85
00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:23.666
<b>and that's why</b>

86
00:05:23.666 --> 00:05:25.500
<b>he has become directionless.</b>

87
00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:27.291
<b>But</b>

88
00:05:27.291 --> 00:05:28.666
<b> what is the</b>

89
00:05:28.666 --> 00:05:32.125
<b>right inspiration?</b>

90
00:05:32.125 --> 00:05:36.208
<b>What should Arjuna do?</b>

91
00:05:36.208 --> 00:05:39.791
<b>What should you do?</b>

92
00:05:39.791 --> 00:05:44.666
<b>The answer to all these lies in our duty.</b>

93
00:05:44.666 --> 00:05:50.166
<b>If we understand our duty well,</b>

94
00:05:50.166 --> 00:05:53.833
<b>then inspiration will return on its own.</b>

95
00:05:53.833 --> 00:05:55.125
<b>But</b>

96
00:05:55.125 --> 00:05:59.083
<b>how to recognize duty?</b>

97
00:05:59.083 --> 00:06:02.291
<b>You will get answers to all your questions.</b>

98
00:06:02.291 --> 00:06:08.541
<b>Just maintain your inspiration</b>
<b>to complete this Gita.</b>

99
00:06:09.041 --> 00:06:13.250


100
00:06:13.250 --> 00:06:15.416
<b>Family is bound by</b>

101
00:06:15.416 --> 00:06:18.000
<b>threads of love.</b>

102
00:06:18.000 --> 00:06:19.333
<b>But</b>

103
00:06:19.333 --> 00:06:20.541
<b>sometimes</b>

104
00:06:20.541 --> 00:06:23.791
<b>these threads get entangled,</b>

105
00:06:23.791 --> 00:06:29.750
<b>these threads get wound around our heart,</b>

106
00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:34.625
<b>our mind in such a way that we become inactive.</b>

107
00:06:34.625 --> 00:06:36.083
<b>What will you do</b>

108
00:06:36.083 --> 00:06:39.333
<b>in such a situation?</b>

109
00:06:39.333 --> 00:06:42.416
<b>And the answer to this lies in another question,</b>

110
00:06:42.416 --> 00:06:44.583
<b>which is,</b>

111
00:06:44.583 --> 00:06:47.500
<b>what are your ideals,</b>

112
00:06:47.500 --> 00:06:50.750
<b> your life values?</b>

113
00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:52.250
<b>Your ideals</b>

114
00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.500
<b>are a foundation</b>

115
00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:55.666
<b>that</b>

116
00:06:55.666 --> 00:06:59.166
<b>keeps your building-like mind stable. </b>

117
00:06:59.166 --> 00:07:00.416
<b>Values</b>

118
00:07:00.416 --> 00:07:04.875
<b>provide your character with</b>
<b>the power of consciousness,</b>

119
00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:08.041
<b>on which millions of waves may break</b>

120
00:07:08.041 --> 00:07:11.416
<b>but it remains steadfast.</b>

121
00:07:11.416 --> 00:07:18.750
<b>Keep assessing and improving</b>
<b>your ideals and your values.</b>

122
00:07:18.750 --> 00:07:25.708
<b>This does not mean at all that you</b>
<b>do not love your family,</b>

123
00:07:25.708 --> 00:07:30.083
<b>love is the essence of life,</b>

124
00:07:30.083 --> 00:07:34.583
<b>But if there is ever a deep entanglement,</b>

125
00:07:34.583 --> 00:07:39.125
<b>then consider your ideals and</b>
<b>values as your pole star,</b>

126
00:07:39.125 --> 00:07:41.583
<b>the way will be found automatically</b>

127
00:07:42.166 --> 00:07:46.291


128
00:07:46.291 --> 00:07:49.458
<b>Arjuna is considering this as personal revenge.</b>

129
00:07:49.458 --> 00:07:50.958
<b>He's thinking</b>

130
00:07:50.958 --> 00:07:54.333
<b>that he shouldn't take this revenge now.</b>

131
00:07:54.333 --> 00:07:55.125
<b>Arjuna</b>

132
00:07:55.125 --> 00:08:00.916
<b>is also viewing the fame and wealth after the war</b>
<b>from a personal perspective. </b>

133
00:08:00.916 --> 00:08:06.041
<b>He thinks he doesn't want fame and wealth at all.	</b>

134
00:08:06.041 --> 00:08:10.958
<b>He's looking at every aspect of</b>
<b>this situation very closely,</b>

135
00:08:10.958 --> 00:08:14.375
<b>from his personal viewpoint,</b>

136
00:08:14.375 --> 00:08:17.916
<b>and that's why he's confused.</b>

137
00:08:17.916 --> 00:08:21.750
<b>But the matter was never personal,</b>

138
00:08:21.750 --> 00:08:24.875
<b>This war is about establishing dharma</b>
<b>(righteousness) in the world. </b>

139
00:08:24.875 --> 00:08:26.166
<b>This war is about </b>

140
00:08:26.166 --> 00:08:29.500
<b>keeping the flame of faith alive in all</b>

141
00:08:29.500 --> 00:08:34.500
<b>those who feel that goodness loses to evil.</b>

142
00:08:34.500 --> 00:08:39.083
<b>Arjuna is also a leader of the army,</b>
<b>of the kingdom.</b>

143
00:08:39.083 --> 00:08:42.166
<b>You too might be in your organization.</b>

144
00:08:42.166 --> 00:08:48.500
<b>Do you look at a situation only from</b>
<b>a personal perspective</b>

145
00:08:48.541 --> 00:08:52.166
<b>or through the eyes of your entire responsibility?</b>

146
00:08:52.166 --> 00:08:55.333
<b>Many colleagues are also dependent on you,</b>

147
00:08:55.333 --> 00:08:57.583
<b>who follow you.</b>

148
00:08:57.583 --> 00:09:01.208
<b>From the perspective of responsibility,</b>
<b>everything becomes clear.</b>

149
00:09:01.208 --> 00:09:02.333
<b>Yes,</b>

150
00:09:02.333 --> 00:09:05.916
<b>emotions can cloud this vision,</b>

151
00:09:05.916 --> 00:09:07.208
<b>so</b>

152
00:09:07.208 --> 00:09:13.333
<b>along with understanding responsibility, </b>
<b>emotional balance is also necessary.</b>

153
00:09:13.333 --> 00:09:16.416
<b>This Gita will support you in that.</b>

154
00:09:16.416 --> 00:09:20.333
<b>This Gita is like the anchor of a ship</b>

155
00:09:20.333 --> 00:09:25.666
<b>that keeps it stable even amidst fierce waves.</b>

